# .gitignore for the gh-pages branch.
#
# gh-pages shares one working directory with main (the deploy recipe
# does `git checkout gh-pages` in the same tree). Switching branches
# removes main's *tracked* files but leaves main's *ignored* build
# artifacts (test binaries, dist/, generated HTML) sitting in the tree.
# Without this file those leak in as untracked on gh-pages and a
# `git add -A` deploy would sweep them into the branch.
#
# Mirror of main's .gitignore so exactly what main ignores, gh-pages
# ignores too. Already-tracked deploy assets (playground.html, the
# *.wasm, ssql_gpu, …) are unaffected — git ignore rules never apply
# to tracked files, so `git add -A` still stages real deploy changes.

*~
*.dll
*.dylib
*.exe
*.exe~
*.out
*.so
*.swo
*.swp
*.test
*_demo
*_example

/dist/
/seq_*
/test_*
/*.html
/*_demo
/*_example

.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
Thumbs.db
go.work
default.pgo

# Stray Go test binaries that leak from the shared tree (e.g. typed.test).
typed/
